The cache is a process-wide (thread-local) LRU of `Rc<DiffModel>` — diff_view.rs:56-60, `static CACHE: RefCell<Vec<(u64, Rc<DiffModel>)>>`, `const CACHE_LIMIT: usize = 16` — and `apply_syntax` mutates the shared model through interior mutability (crates/fleet-lazygit/src/views/diff_model.rs:457-464), so the cached `Rc` and the installed one are the same object. `reload` short-circuits on a cache hit and starts no task at all — diff_view.rs:403-406:
```rust
if let Some(model) = cached(self.key) {
    self.model = Some(model);
    return;
}
```
`self.cancelled.store(true, …)` at diff_view.rs:400 (start of `reload`) and `impl Drop for DiffView` at diff_view.rs:310-314 are exactly what makes the two early returns above reachable.

